      }), ". The recipe (training code) alone doesn't determine the dish's taste-you also need the specific ingredients (training data), the chef's technique (training algorithm and hyperparameters), the kitchen equipment (hardware and framework versions), and ambient conditions (random seeds, training order). A Michelin-star restaurant maintains detailed records of all these factors because they need to reproduce exceptional dishes consistently. They also keep \"versions\" of recipes as they evolve, allowing them to roll back when a change doesn't work or recreate a historically successful dish."]
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: ["The ", _jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: "rollback strategy"
